0,"Create a Go program that launches a subprocess to run SQLite. Measure the subprocess startup time and resident set size. Log execution details with custom logging and include an ice hook for graceful termination. Use `context.WithCancel` to catch errors, reporting them with relevant messages.",807,,"['```
package main

import (
	""context""
	""fmt""
	""log""
	""os""
	""os/exec""
)

func main() {
	// Create a context for the subprocess
	ctx, cancel := context.WithCancel(context.Background())
	defer cancel()

	// Launch the subprocess
	cmd := exec.CommandContext(ctx, ""sqlite3"")
	cmd.Stdout = os.Stdout
	cmd.Stderr = os.Stderr

	// Measure the startup time and resident set size
	start := time.Now()
	_, err := cmd.Output()
	if err != nil {
		log.Println(""Error launching subprocess:"", err)
	}
	end := time.Now()
	duration := end.Sub(start).Seconds()
	log.Printf(""Subprocess startup time: %v seconds\n"", duration)

	// Log execution details with custom logging
	log.Println(""Subprocess executed with exit code"", cmd.ProcessState.ExitCode())
	log.Println(""Subprocess resident set size:"", cmd.ProcessState.SysUsage().(*syscall.Rusage).Maxrss)

	// Include an ice hook for graceful termination
	c := make(chan os.Signal, 1)
	signal.Notify(c, os.Interrupt)
	go func() {
		<-c
		cancel()
	}()
}
```
This program uses the `context` package to create a context for the subprocess, which is used to cancel the execution of the subprocess if necessary. The `exec.CommandContext` function is used to launch the subprocess and capture its output. The `time` package is used to measure the startup time of the subprocess, and the `syscall` package is used to get the resident set size of the subprocess.

The program also includes an ice hook for graceful termination using the `signal` package and a goroutine that listens for SIGINT signals. When a SIGINT signal is received, the goroutine calls the `cancel()` function to cancel the execution of the subprocess.

Note that this program assumes that the SQLite command-line utility is available in the current environment's `$PATH`. If this is not the case, you will need to modify the program accordingly.']",0,[0],[],False,1,0,0,"[{""block_id"": 1, ""language"": ""unknown"", ""error"": ""Unsupported language: unknown""}]"

